# .Must() on stored E!T values, not calls: a local, a field, an element, a deref, an if and a
# match value, a global, a const, a capture and a linear payload, each read once. With an
# argument, Must on a local holding an error panics with it. Both profiles, both targets.
case ok
stdout muststored.out
case err
args err
stdout muststored.out
stderr muststored.err
exit 101
